alue "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SWM'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Swimming at the 2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "16 – 23 September 2000"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/758"} "Sydney International Aquatic Centre, Olympic Park, Sydney, New South Wales"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Perhaps no other country in the world uses swimming as a benchmark for sporting success more than Australia so it was no surprise that the sport became a focus for public and media attention in Sydney. It also helped that Australia had their strongest team in a generation spearheaded by " [:a {:href "/athletes/93263"} "Grant Hackett"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/45105"} "Susie O’Neill"] " and a supremely talented teenager named " [:a {:href "/athletes/93280"} "Ian Thorpe"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It took Thorpe little time to make an indelible impression on the Games as by the end of the first day on competition he had already collected two Olympic titles. His two golds, in the 400 metres freestyle and 4 x 200 freestyle relay were both achieved in world record time but in much different circumstances. Thorpe’s individual win was quite straightforward but the relay was achieved only when he produced an improbable comeback on the final leg to beat the American team. In all he won five medals, three gold and two silver, and emerged as one of the stars of the Games."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three men completed the 100/200 double, " [:a {:href "/athletes/49500"} "Pieter van den Hoogenband"] " in freestyle, " [:a {:href "/athletes/93557"} "Domenico Fioravanti"] " in breaststroke and " [:a {:href "/athletes/93856"} "Lenny Krayzelburg"] " in backstroke. Krayzelburg was the only man to match Thorpe’s gold medal tally after adding a medley relay title to his collection."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The outstanding female swimmer of the Games was Dutchwoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/49315"} "Inge de Bruijn"] " who won three individual golds whilst " [:a {:href "/athletes/93722"} "Diana Mocanu"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/50965"} "Brooke Bennett"] "  and " [:a {:href "/athletes/93833"} "Yana Klochkova"] " each won two titles.  The other swimmer to win three gold medals was American " [:a {:href "/athletes/51217"} "Jenny Thompson"] " who took her career total to eight, each one having been won as part of a relay team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Making his Olympic début was a 15-year-old American named " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " who placed fifth in the 200 metres butterfly. The world would hear more from him in the decade to come."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The USA topped the medal table with 14 gold medals and 33 in total which was some way ahead of Australia.  This began a three Olympic stretch where the two countries would be clearly the strongest nations in the sport."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/8336"} "50 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "21 – 22 September 2000"] "\n" [:td {} "77"] "\n" [:td {} "71"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/8352"} "100 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "19 – 20 September 2000"] "\n" [:td {} "73"] "\n" [:td {} "66"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/8368"} "200 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "17 – 18 September 2000"] "\n" [:td {} "51"] "\n" [:td {} "44"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/8381"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "16 September 2000"] "\n" [:td {} "46"] "\n" [:td {} "40"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/8390"} "1,500 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "22 – 23 September 2000"] "\n" [:td {} "41"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/